    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe mamba checkpoint pool builds its conv buffers from the logical layout (`cache_params.shape.conv`, `(d, k)`), but the active pool may allocate conv windows transposed — the NPU backend allocates `(k, d)` to match its kernels. Copying conv states between the two pools then fails with a broadcast error, breaking `--enable-int8-mamba-checkpoint` on Ascend NPU in **both** directions:\r\n\r\n- `store_from_active` (radix cache store):\r\n\r\n  ```\r\n  RuntimeError: shape mismatch: value tensor of shape [30, 1, 3, 4096] cannot be broadcast to indexing result of shape [30, 1, 4096, 3]\r\n  ```\r\n\r\n- `load_to_active` (cache-hit copy-on-write): the mirror-image error (`[30, 1, 4096, 3]` → `[30, 1, 3, 4096]`)\r\n\r\nThis is a completeness gap of the unified ssm-state-layout refactor (#36187): the active pool layout and kernels were updated, but the checkpoint pool copy path was missed. Note #43072 (int8 e2e test) would hit the same crash on NPU.\r\n\r\n## Modification\r\n\r\nMake both copy sites layout-adaptive: transpose when the last two dims do not match. When the layouts already agree (e.g. CUDA), the condition is false and the code path is unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Accuray Test\r\n\r\nAscend 910C (A3, CANN 9.1.0, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, TP2), `test_int8_delays_prefix_reuse_collapse` — **OK**:\r\n\r\n| | K=64 | K=128 | K=256 | K=512 |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| int8 off | 0.984 | 0.984 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\r\n| int8 on  | 0.984 | 0.984 | 0.984 | 0.863 |\r\n\r\nint8 checkpoint delays the prefix-reuse collapse point from K=256 to K=512+, as designed.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\n<!-- If this pull request impacts inference speed, provide benchmarking and profiling results. -->\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38241770203](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38241770203)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38241769835](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38241769835)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38241770213](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38241770213)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
